{
  "about": [
    "The per-placement blobs of a placement row, as the game's native serializers write them (placement_params.h).",
    "Generate placement_layouts.h from this file with tools/navigation/make_placement_layouts.py.",
    "A slot is one blob of a row: its fields start every layout of the slot. A slot with a chain also takes the parts of",
    "the classes of the actor's native class chain (actor) or its AI component's (component), walked from the base class",
    "down: a part with base replace replaces the stream of the classes above it, one with base inherit appends to it.",
    "A part with variants has several layouts, tried in order when a blob is read.",
    "A field's type is a scalar (bool i32 u32 f32 u8 u16 u64 name vec rot quat) or one of the types. An item @Name in a",
    "field list is the fields of that list. Gates compare the row version: > above, < below, = equal.",
    "derived: no property holds the field; a writer gives it runtime_default, or count_of (the item count of the owner",
    "property), component_tag (a run of the world locations of the actor's scene components with that tag, in the",
    "actor's component order, as many as its counter says) or component_transform (the actor's component of the field's",
    "name; the field is there only when the actor has it) say how it is filled.",
    "drops: an array of drops; drop_key: its drops are generators of their own, numbered from the list with keys of the actor,",
    "this word and their place, and listed in the sibling drop_list. Drops without drop_key get no number.",
    "A slot's owner is the component its blob is read from: the one the actor's property holds when it is of one of the",
    "classes, else the first component of the first class that has one, not of except. An owner with no classes is the actor."
  ],
